  "title": "Chapter 9 – Hand Tools and Their Uses",
  "order": 9,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "76dv90t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Hand tools are classified by function into striking, driving, holding, cutting, and measuring tools.",
        "Ball-peen hammers are specified by weight and shape of the peen, widely used for riveting.",
        "Files are specified by length, grade, cut, and shape, made from high carbon steel.",
        "Hacksaw blades made of High-Speed Steel (HSS) cut metal efficiently depending on tooth pitch selection.",
        "Cold chisels are hardened and tempered at the cutting edge to chip or sever cold metals."
      ],
      "id": "ttrqi1d"
    },
